    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## str and String\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`str` is UTF-8 text, a view (`&str` is `str`, as `&[T]` is `[T]`); a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"string literal is one where a `str` goes, and a `str` goes where a `[u8]`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"does, for free. `String` owns its text, on an allocator:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`String::new_in(gpa)`, `String::from_in(\"x\", gpa)`, `s.push_str(\"..\")`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`s.push(c)` (a code point, a `u32`: vole has no `char` yet),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`s.push_fmt(\"{x}\")`, `to_string_in(format_args(\"..\", y), gpa)`. A String has its\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`str`'s methods (`s.trim()`), and `&s` goes where a `str` or `[u8]` does.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"The methods are Rust's, and what they return views the text: `len`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`chars()` (code points; `.rev()`), `char_indices()`, `bytes()`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`lines()`, `split(p)`, `splitn(n, p)`, `split_once(p)`, `rsplit_once`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`split_whitespace()`, `trim()` (and `_start`, `_end`, `_matches`),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`strip_prefix(p)`, `starts_with(p)`, `ends_with`, `contains`, `find(p)`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(an `Option<i64>`, a byte index), `rfind`, `matches(p)`, `parse::<T>()`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"(numbers, `bool`), `width()` (terminal columns), `graphemes(true)`. A\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"pattern `p` is a `str` (`\", \"`), a byte (`','`) or a code point (`0x4e16\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"as u32`). What allocates takes an allocator, Rust's name with `_in`:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`to_uppercase_in(gpa)`, `to_lowercase_in`, `replace_in(a, b, gpa)`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`repeat_in(n, gpa)`, `to_string_in(gpa)`, `.collect_in(gpa)`; the Rust\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"forms are errors naming them. Bytes become a `str` checked:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`str::from_utf8(b)?`, `String::from_utf8(v)?` (a `Vec<u8, Gpa>`),\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`String::from_buf(b)?`, `String::from_utf8_lossy_in(b, gpa)`; back:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`s.as_bytes()`, `s.into_bytes()`, `s.into_buf()`. (0.25.5) Bytes (any\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"slice whose elements have `==`) have `starts_with(p)` and `ends_with(p)`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"too: `name.ends_with(\".vl\")` of a `[u8]`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn initials(name: str, gpa: Gpa) -> String<Gpa> {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var out = String::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    for w in name.split_whitespace() {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        out.push(w.chars().next().unwrap());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main(gpa: Gpa) -> i32 {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let line: str = \"  ada lovelace, 1815 \";\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let (name, year) = line.trim().split_once(\", \").unwrap();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let born = year.parse::<i64>().unwrap();\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let up = name.to_uppercase_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let short = initials(name, gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{up} {short} {} {}\", 2026 - born, name.contains('l'));\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let parts: Vec<str, Gpa> = \"a,b,,c\".split(',').collect_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{parts:?} {}\", parts.len());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    0\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"ADA LOVELACE al 211 true\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"[\"a\", \"b\", \"\", \"c\"] 4\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## String constants\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"String constants come in four forms:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| form | what it is |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"|---|---|\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `const X: str = \"...\";` | text, a value: each use is the literal (0.25.4); a text block too |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `const X: [u8] = \"...\";` | bytes; a text block (`\"\"\"`, `guide syntax#lexical`), `include_str(\"f.wgsl\")` and `include_bytes(\"f.bin\")` too |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `static X: str = \"...\";` | text in a place, one address for every use, as any static |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `static X: [str; N] = [\"a\", \"b\"];` | an array of them (`const` too): `X[i]` is one, `X[..]` the slice; `[str]`, without the length, is refused |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"What turns one form into another:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| you have | you want | write |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"|---|---|---|\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| a `str` (a literal, a static) | `[u8]` | nothing: a `str` goes where a `[u8]` does; `s.as_bytes()` says so |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `[u8]` | `str` | `str::from_utf8(b)?`: checked, a `Result` |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| `Vec<T, A>`, `Buf` | `[T]`, `[u8]` | `v.as_slice()`, a view, no copy; a `String`: `s.as_str()` |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| a format string | its text | `format_in(\"..\", args, gpa)`, a `String<A>` (`.as_str()` views it; 0.26.3: a `Buf` before); `to_string_in(x, gpa)` for one value |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"| a slice | appended | `v.extend_from_slice(s)` to a `Vec`; `push_str(s)` to a `Buf` or `String` |\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`print`, `println` and `eprintln` take any `T: Display`: a number, a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`str`, a `[u8]`, `format_args(..)`, with no allocator; a literal first\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"is a format string, its arguments after it. (0.26.2) `panic(\"bad {x}\")`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"and `assert(c, \"bad {}\", x)` format their message too, on the stack, with\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"no allocator; a message that is no literal is a `[u8]` (a `str` too).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"const SHADER: [u8] = \"\"\"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    @compute @workgroup_size(1)\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    fn main() {}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    \"\"\";\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"const NAME: str = \"vole\";\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"static DAYS: [str; 3] = [\"mon\", \"tue\", \"wed\"];\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main(gpa: Gpa) {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let bytes: [u8] = NAME; // a str goes where [u8] does\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let text: str = str::from_utf8(SHADER).unwrap(); // bytes to str: checked\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var v: Vec<u8, Gpa> = Vec::new_in(gpa);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.extend_from_slice(NAME.as_bytes());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    v.extend_from_slice(DAYS[1]);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let msg = format_in(\"{NAME}: {} days, {} bytes\", DAYS.len(), v.len(), gpa); // a String\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(msg.as_slice());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(\"{} {} {}\", bytes.len, text.lines().count(), DAYS[..].len());\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    if v.len() != 7 {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"        panic(msg.as_slice()); // a [u8]: no format string\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    }\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"vole: 3 days, 7 bytes\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"4 2 3\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"## Numbers as text without an allocator\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`format_in(\"{v:.2}\", gpa)` allocates a `String`; a loop that writes a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"number every frame (a UI's label) writes it into a stack array instead.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`std::num::fmt_f64(v, decimals, &out)` (0.25.4) writes `{v:.N}`'s text\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"byte for byte at the end of a `[u8; 32]` and returns where it starts:\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"the exact value rounded to the nearest, a tie to the even digit (`2.5`\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"to 0 decimals is `2`, as C's `%.0f` and Rust's `{:.0}`), `-0.00`,\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`NaN`, `inf`; `decimals` from 0 to `FIXED_DECIMALS_MAX` (20); a text\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"longer than 32 bytes is `{v:e}`'s. An `f32` is `fmt_f64(x as f64, ..)`.\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`fmt_i64(v, &out)` and `fmt_u64` do the same for integers into a\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"`[u8; 20]` (`guide formatting#numbers`).\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```vole\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"use std::num::{fmt_f64, fmt_i64};\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"fn main() {\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var out: [u8; 32] = [0; 32];\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let at = fmt_f64(3.14159, 2, &out);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(out[at..32]);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let at2 = fmt_f64(-0.5, 0, &out);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(out[at2..32]);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    var digits: [u8; 20] = [0; 20];\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    let i = fmt_i64(-42, &digits);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"    println(digits[i..20]);\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"}\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```out\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"3.14\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"-0\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"-42\n");
    buf_bytes(out, b"```\n");
}
